            "review_title": "Review at Mai Xuan Canh",
            "review_text": "Goochmaster\nSydney, Australia1887 contributions\n0\nLocal Food that's hard to find.\nFeb 2017 • Friends\nThe locals tell me this place is where you go for local food. It's near the Notre Dame church and close by to places in District 1. District 1 is safe for walking however you can get bag snatched elsewhere easily.\n\nChicken Pho is clearly good value and tastes fresh. They use glass style noodle. Grilled chicken, splits chicken feet all mixed in with salt and lime. A meal for 4 people cost $25USD.\n\nYou come into this tiled alley and they unpack plastic tables and chairs for you. Whilst you eat, scooters drive by to the house at the back. Basically you are eating in an alleyway. \n\nCome here for local street food that's authentic which you don't need to worry about hygiene and foreigners who have grown up in sterile environments like Australia or U.K. should be able to consume.\n\nI walked back to Novotel in less than 10 minutes and can stop for Ice Cream along the way.\n\nDon't come here for a business meeting, it's a real local eating joint and just how they eat across Indo China like Cambodia and Thailand.\n\nI've been warned the servers are grumpy but the food is good.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten February 22, 2017",
